@startuml usecase
title COLORS Web Application - Use Case Diagram

left to right direction
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam usecase {
  BackgroundColor #F8F8F8
  BorderColor #555555
}

actor "User\n(seeded account)" as User
actor "MySQL Database\n(COP4331)" as DB <<system>>

rectangle "COLORS Web Application" {
  usecase "Log In" as UC_Login
  usecase "Hash Password (MD5)" as UC_Hash
  usecase "Start Session\n(save 20-min cookie,\ngo to color.html)" as UC_Session
  usecase "Show Login Error" as UC_LoginErr

  usecase "Search Colors" as UC_Search
  usecase "Add Color" as UC_Add
  usecase "Log Out" as UC_Logout
  usecase "Clear Session Cookie" as UC_Clear
}

User --> UC_Login
User --> UC_Search
User --> UC_Add
User --> UC_Logout

UC_Login ..> UC_Hash : <<include>>
UC_Session ..> UC_Login : <<extend>>\n[credentials match]
UC_LoginErr ..> UC_Login : <<extend>>\n[no matching user]
UC_Logout ..> UC_Clear : <<include>>

UC_Login --> DB : SELECT Users
UC_Search --> DB : SELECT Colors\n(Name LIKE, UserID)
UC_Add --> DB : INSERT Colors

note right of UC_Search
  Search Colors, Add Color, and Log Out are
  only reachable from color.html, which calls
  readCookie() on load and redirects to
  index.html when there is no userId cookie.
  Every color query is scoped to the user's ID.
end note

note bottom of UC_Login
  There is no sign-up use case:
  accounts are seeded directly in SQL.
  The Contacts table exists in the schema
  but no use case reads or writes it.
end note

@enduml
